		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: DM-8 battery poor fit on GD-77]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4987&amp;p=36399#p36399"><![CDATA[
Thanks for telling us your fix!  I suppose the slots on the battery are the only place that it can bind up so enlarging them makes sense.  I took the old battery, flipped it front to back just so I could slip it's slots onto the radio's tabs and it slipped on and off easily.  Not so much with the new one.  After repeated cycles of slipping the new battery on and off the fit is improving.  A small detail to be sure, but it's no bueno when the battery falls off in the middle of a qso.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2079">k7xta</a> — Mon Mar 24, 2025 12:35 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
